@startuml
title A Tag Names a Handler — One MeTTaIL Mechanism at Two Levels
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #334155

rectangle "**Level 1 — Foreign Language Term**\n(FLT FIPS, 2026-06-26)" as FLT #F8FAFC {
  rectangle "the //element//\n""lam`App(${f}, K)`""\n""perl:Str{ &#34;hello&#34; }""" as FLTex #BFDBFE
  rectangle "the tag ""lam"" selects\n**a guest grammar + reflector**\nkeyed by the fingerprint <latex>\mathcal{F}</latex>" as FLTres #DDD6FE
  rectangle "what is interpreted:\n**raw guest source**, bounded by\nan author-chosen delimiter" as FLTel #BFDBFE
}

rectangle "**Level 2 — Language specification**\n(this FIPS)" as SPEC #F8FAFC {
  rectangle "the //element//\n""(&#34;arrow&#34;, &#34;Term&#34;, &#34;Term&#34;)""\n""(&#34;App&#34;, &#34;M0&#34;, &#34;N&#34;)""" as SPECex #E0E7FF
  rectangle "the tag ""&#34;arrow&#34;"" selects\n**an elaborator arm**\nfrom a closed, versioned set" as SPECres #DDD6FE
  rectangle "what is interpreted:\n**an already-parsed Rholang value**" as SPECel #E0E7FF
}

rectangle "**The unforgeable realisation**\n<latex>\ulcorner \mathcal{F} \cdot L \urcorner \;=\; \texttt{GPrivate}(\texttt{mettail.term.}\mathcal{F}\texttt{.}L)</latex>\n""reflect_tag"" in rholang-codegen/src/rho_net_lower.rs" as TAG #FBCFE8

FLTex --> FLTres : names
FLTres --> FLTel : interprets
SPECex --> SPECres : names
SPECres --> SPECel : interprets

FLTres -[#BE185D]-> TAG : resolved through
SPECres -[#BE185D]-> TAG : **installs** the tags\nthat level 1 resolves

note bottom of TAG #FBCFE8
  A conventional namespace can be squatted; a ""GPrivate"" derived from
  the definition fingerprint cannot — //given an injective// <latex>\mathcal{F}</latex>. Cross-language
  matching therefore fails **closed**: a mismatch is a //non//-firing, never a
  //wrong// firing. §IX.2 states the exact scope of that guarantee, and §IX.3 R-1
  records the one way it can be defeated: a fingerprint collision, which is
  why W-7 makes <latex>\mathcal{F}</latex> a wide cryptographic digest before any specification
  of non-local provenance may elaborate.
end note

note as N #F1F5F9
  **Where the two levels differ, honestly.** Level 1 interprets //source text//, so it is a
  reader-level construct and inherits the modal-lexer delimiter obligations catalogued in
  the FLT FIPS — fence run lengths, heredoc words, escape tracking. Level 2 interprets
  //values//, so it needs no lexer at all: Rholang's parser has produced the value before any
  tag is examined. The shared content is the resolution discipline —
  <latex>\tau \cdot e \mapsto H(\tau)(e)</latex> with <latex>H</latex> keyed by an unforgeable identity — not the syntax.
end note

